{
  "assessment": "The source packet provides a complete experimental and theoretical description of the unitary almost-Mathieu operator (UAMO) and its non-Hermitian extension (PUAMO) realized via single-photon quantum walks. The selected quantitative cluster focuses on the Lyapunov exponent L_lambda1_lambda2_eta of the PUAMO, which is given by L = max(0, log(lambda_0) - 2*pi*|eta|) with lambda_0 = lambda_2*(1+lambda_1')/(lambda_1*(1+lambda_2')). Two claims are built for the private regimes eta=0 and eta=0.1, sharing public controls lambda_1 and lambda_2 in [0.2,0.67] and the common readout lyapunov_exponent. The source reports the full parameter-space phase scans for the Hermitian (eta=0) and non-Hermitian (eta=0.1) cases, and the Lyapunov formula is explicitly given in the supplementary material. The extraction captures the central quantitative relation with all structural constants as named, anchored parameters. The source contains an internal inconsistency in the PT-threshold wording: the main text states eta_PT = -log(lambda_0) (line 125) and Methods repeats eta = -log(lambda_0) (line 211), while the supplementary dual exponent formula at line 359 and the reported numeric value 0.119 for lambda_1=0.25, lambda_2=0.5 (line 152) imply eta_PT = log(lambda_0)/(2*pi). This inconsistency does not affect the selected Lyapunov equations, which are internally consistent. Therefore case_authoring_ready is set to true.",
